<title>USA: Central Maine Power says 4,000 still without power.</title>
<headline>Central Maine Power says 4,000 still without power.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Maine 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Maine Power said Monday 4,000 of its customers remained without power after a weekend storm pounded New England, leaving up to 18 inches of heavy, wet snow.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the utility said 30 extra work crews from New Brunswick, Canada, had been brought in to help restore power.</p>
<p>He expected power to be fully restored by the end of the day.</p>
<p>--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106</p>
